/*
 * File: rsdlwin.ri - SDL3 specific graphics routines
 *
 * All drawing goes to a software canvas (src/common/ucanvas.c); windows
 * on screen (src/common/usdlwin.c) just display it.  The canvas plays
 * the role of the X backend's backing pixmap, so a window can be hidden,
 * resized or covered without losing its contents, and pixel reads,
 * copies and drawing operations are the same on every platform.
 *
 * The structure and the semantics follow rxwin.ri, so that programs
 * behave the same way they do under X11.
 */

